#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:414
msgid "``rotate`` - Delete outdated distribution files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:416
msgid ""
"As you develop new versions of your project, your distribution (``dist``) "
"directory will gradually fill up with older source and/or binary "
"distribution files.  The ``rotate`` command lets you automatically clean "
"these up, keeping only the N most-recently modified files matching a given "
"pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:421
msgid "``--match=PATTERNLIST, -m PATTERNLIST``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:422
msgid ""
"Comma-separated list of glob patterns to match.  This option is *required*. "
"The project name and ``-*`` is prepended to the supplied patterns, in order "
"to match only distributions belonging to the current project (in case you "
"have a shared distribution directory for multiple projects).  Typically, you "
"will use a glob pattern like ``.zip`` or ``.egg`` to match files of the "
"specified type.  Note that each supplied pattern is treated as a distinct "
"group of files for purposes of selecting files to delete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:430
msgid "``--keep=COUNT, -k COUNT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:431
msgid ""
"Number of matching distributions to keep.  For each group of files "
"identified by a pattern specified with the ``--match`` option, delete all "
"but the COUNT most-recently-modified files in that group.  This option is "
"*required*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:437
msgid ""
"Directory where the distributions are.  This defaults to the value of the "
"``bdist`` command's ``--dist-dir`` option, which will usually be the "
"project's ``dist`` subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:441
msgid ""
"**Example 1**: Delete all .tar.gz files from the distribution directory, "
"except for the 3 most recently modified ones::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:444
msgid "setup.py rotate --match=.tar.gz --keep=3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:446
msgid ""
"**Example 2**: Delete all Python 2.3 or Python 2.4 eggs from the "
"distribution directory, except the most recently modified one for each "
