#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:455
msgid "``saveopts`` - Save used options to a configuration file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:457
msgid ""
"Finding and editing ``distutils`` configuration files can be a pain, "
"especially since you also have to translate the configuration options from "
"command-line form to the proper configuration file format.  You can avoid "
"these hassles by using the ``saveopts`` command.  Just add it to the command "
"line to save the options you used.  For example, this command builds the "
"project using the ``mingw32`` C compiler, then saves the --compiler setting "
"as the default for future builds (even those run implicitly by the "
"``install`` command)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:465
msgid "setup.py build --compiler=mingw32 saveopts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:467
msgid ""
"The ``saveopts`` command saves all options for every command specified on "
"the command line to the project's local ``setup.cfg`` file, unless you use "
"one of the `configuration file options`_ to change where the options are "
"saved.  For example, this command does the same as above, but saves the "
"compiler setting to the site-wide (global) distutils configuration::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:473
msgid "setup.py build --compiler=mingw32 saveopts -g"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:475
msgid ""
"Note that it doesn't matter where you place the ``saveopts`` command on the "
"command line; it will still save all the options specified for all commands. "
"For example, this is another valid way to spell the last example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:479
msgid "setup.py saveopts -g build --compiler=mingw32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:481
msgid ""
"Note, however, that all of the commands specified are always run, regardless "
"of where ``saveopts`` is placed on the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:486
msgid "Configuration File Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:488
msgid ""
"Normally, settings such as options and aliases are saved to the project's "
"local ``setup.cfg`` file.  But you can override this and save them to the "
"global or per-user configuration files, or to a manually-specified filename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:492
msgid "``--global-config, -g``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:493
msgid ""
"Save settings to the global ``distutils.cfg`` file inside the ``distutils`` "
"package directory.  You must have write access to that directory to use this "
"option.  You also can't combine this option with ``-u`` or ``-f``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:497
msgid "``--user-config, -u``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:498
msgid ""
"Save settings to the current user's ``~/.pydistutils.cfg`` (POSIX) or "
"``$HOME/pydistutils.cfg`` (Windows) file.  You can't combine this option "
"with ``-g`` or ``-f``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:502
msgid "``--filename=FILENAME, -f FILENAME``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:503
msgid ""
"Save settings to the specified configuration file to use.  You can't combine "
"this option with ``-g`` or ``-u``.  Note that if you specify a non-standard "
"filename, the ``distutils`` and ``setuptools`` will not use the file's "
"contents.  This option is mainly included for use in testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:509
msgid ""
"These options are used by other ``setuptools`` commands that modify "
"configuration files, such as the `alias`_ and `setopt`_ commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:516
msgid "``setopt`` - Set a distutils or setuptools option in a config file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:518
msgid ""
"This command is mainly for use by scripts, but it can also be used as a "
"quick and dirty way to change a distutils configuration option without "
"having to remember what file the options are in and then open an editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/commands.rst:522
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.  Set the default C compiler to ``mingw32`` (using long option "
"names)::"
